WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.180
Many fans of One Piece predict that someday
Marco the Phoenix will die and be reborn in

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.180
the series.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.460
But what if I told you he already has.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:16.600
It’s a hot, hot summer, ooor winter, depending
when and and where you’re watching this,

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:22.890
anyways, SUMMER - the season of backyard barbecues
and it’s time to slice up one of our favorite,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.480
most shareable fruits.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.910
No, I’m not talking about watermelons - I’m
talking about our very favorite pineapple:

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.210
Marco the Phoenix.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.870
By the way, did you know that an old name
for pineapple in Japanese is the “phoenix

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:41.089
pear” - there goes Oda, never missing the
opportunity for some good play.

00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:47.440
But the real question remains: Does Marco
belong on pizza?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.929
Marco the Phoenix has been a fan favorite
One Piece character ever since his debut.

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:57.920
In the 5th, 6th, and 7th One Piece popularity
polls, this character was ranked 12th, 20th,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.920
and 19th respectively.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:08.400
And it’s pretty impressive to break the
top 20 in a series with well over 1,000 named

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.400
characters.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.780
In fact, he’s the 2nd most popular Whitebeard
Pirate after Ace.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:20.549
His own captain, the strongest man in the
world, Whitebeard himself, only made 31st

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:22.409
place in the latest poll.

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:27.560
Sure, Edward Newgate has been absent from
the series for over a decade ever since his

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.439
untimely death, but the strongest man in the
world surely made an impression on the fanbase

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:34.010
to say the least.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.960
I should say Marco’s been a fan favorite
ever since his “proper” debut, once we

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.250
got to see him in action at the Paramount
War.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:46.330
His cameo as a background character during
Whitebeard and Shanks’s meeting hardly counts.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.900
Not only was his character not fleshed out
yet, but his hair color wasn’t even pinned

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.420
down.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:58.140
We had yet to know the sheer volume of cool
that would ooze from this character’s amazing

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.409
devil fruit power.

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:06.280
The tori tori no mi: Model Phoenix was the
first mythical zoan we were ever introduced

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:11.560
to in the series (followed soon after by Sengoku’s
Golden Buddha fruit).

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.500
And no, we’re not counting the Nika fruit
since it wasn’t “formally” introduced

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.270
until very recently.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.750
Why is Marco so endearing to the fanbase?

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:28.530
Sure, he has an awesome power, but that alone
can’t justify his wild popularity among

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.560
a cast with so many fantastically written
characters.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.220
I mean, not only does he outrank Whitebeard
among the fanbase, but heavy hitters like

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.670
Blackbeard, Garp, and Doflamingo.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:45.950
It’s not just the powers of the phoenix,
but the meaning behind the phoenix and how

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:52.150
Marco embodies that meaning that delivers
this character to such heights -

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:58.720
(the heights of popularity, not the kind of
heights he achieves by, you know, flying up

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.720
there).

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:05.290
Someday in the final saga, we may get to see
Marco die and resurrect literally, as many

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:11.710
predict the phoenix fruit will allow him to
do, however, I want to theorize that in a

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:17.690
way, Marco already has died and resurrected
- and in doing so, has shown what it really

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.370
takes to be the first mate of an Emperor of
the Sea.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.510
Oh also, quick shout out to Patrisha and Austin
Singer, both of whom are subscribed to the

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:31.040
channel and thus have helped us increase our
bounty by 100 Berries each, advancing us on

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:36.190
our shared mission to overtake Trebol’s
bounty and reach 100M berries.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.190
Zoro.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.190
Rayleigh.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.190
Katakuri.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.190
Marco.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:45.470
So often in One Piece, the first mates are
the “coolest” characters on their crews

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.230
and in the story overall.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:55.560
Many fans would rank Zoro as their favorite
Straw Hat over Luffy due to his epic three-sword

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.640
style feats.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.730
Rayleigh stopped an admiral’s lightspeed
kick with a sandal.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.900
Katakuri’s design initially looked so edgy
that he seemed out of place in One Piece,

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.490
but he quickly became a beloved antagonist.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.380
When I say these characters are “cool”
I don’t just mean they’re awesome - which

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.430
they are.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:19.430
These characters all have subdued personalities
partnered with effortless feats of brutal

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.430
strength.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.400
They are laid-back in the face of danger.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.510
They ooze “cool”.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:29.900
But is that what makes a first mate?

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.280
No, it takes a lot more than being cool to
be the first mate to the world’s greatest

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.280
pirates.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:40.950
Each of these pirates carries the burden when
their captains no longer can.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:45.820
When their captains are absent or incapacitated,
they are leaders to their crews.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:48.970
They inherit the will of their captains.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.870
When Luffy was unconscious on Thriller Bark,
Zoro took on his pain in order to save the

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:59.770
crew - and he did so unselfishly, proclaiming
that “nothing happened.”

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:04.670
After Roger’s execution, Rayleigh waited
decades on Sabaody Archipelago until he found

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.650
his captain’s successor.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.820
He trained Luffy so that he would stand a
chance on the journey ahead in the New World

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:13.750
and eventually find Laugh Tale.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.510
During Big Mom’s hunger pangs, when she
destroys her own island and even devours her

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:24.780
own children, it’s Katakuri who protects
his family members at all costs.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.700
And Marco, too, carries on the will of Whitebeard.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.990
In doing so, he embodies the spirit of his
devil fruit: the phoenix.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:39.980
In the legend of the phoenix, this fiery bird
makes its nest and dies engulfed in flames.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:45.770
From the ashes that remain, it is reborn as
an egg, hatching again into a new phoenix.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.840
Which is why we have to ask ourselves at this
point in the story whether Baron Tamago has

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.810
a technically more accurate phoenix fruit.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:59.770
On a more serious note, though, it’s fitting
that this story would fit so neatly into mythology.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:05.900
After all, we know Oda loves drawing on various
myths from around the world.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:10.830
The journey of the phoenix can be found in
legends all across the world.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:16.490
The journey of Marco actually parallels a
literary concept called the monomyth.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:21.510
The scholar Joseph Campbell, in his book The
Hero with a Thousand Faces recognized that

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:26.260
many myths and legends from across the world
shared similar structures.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:31.380
This shared, common structure for stories
is called the “monomyth” or the “hero’s

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.380
journey”.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:37.230
One focal part of the “hero’s journey”
comes after great challenges - they fall into

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.940
an abyss, an absolute low point: a death and
rebirth.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:45.700
Ultimately, after their rebirth they rise
into overcoming their challenges and finding

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.360
atonement.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:52.260
The entirety of Luffy’s story mirrors the
hero’s journey very well, too.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:58.210
His lowest point was losing Ace at Marineford,
a period of utter despair and hopelessness

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:01.480
that he was “reborn” from after the timeskip.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.790
But we also see this concept represented in
miniature with Marco, and the legend of the

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.919
phoenix in general.

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:12.860
After the war at Marineford, when the Whitebeard
Pirates lost both their captain and Ace, Marco

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.790
stepped up to the role of leader.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:20.790
As the new captain, he sought vengeance against
Blackbeard, the traitor who had caused unspeakable

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.699
damage to his former crew.

00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:27.230
However, in this Payback War, the remnants
of the Whitebeard Pirates suffered a devastating

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:30.390
loss and subsequently disbanded.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:36.430
If Marco’s journey parallels the mythology
of the phoenix, then this is his death.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:42.560
While once he soared into battle, he went
out in a blaze of glory, seemingly completely

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.560
defeated.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.419
It was then that he retreated to Sphinx Island.

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:51.310
Even after the end of his crew, he never lost
sight of fulfilling his captain’s will.

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:55.740
Marco protected the island that Whitebeard
considered his treasure, using his medical

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:00.880
knowledge to take care of the people there,
and watching over the graves of Ace and his

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:01.880
captain.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:08.400
Though his battle had ended, embers remained
in the ashes - still burning softly with the

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.470
dreams of the late Edward Newgate.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:16.720
In Wano, the phoenix would rise again.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:23.030
Reuniting with another former division commander,
Izo, Marco returned to the battlefield.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:27.490
After hearing Nekomamushi’s plea, he knew
it’s what Whitebeard would have done to

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.699
help avenge his old friend, Kozuki Oden.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:32.930
Now with stylish new glasses

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:39.399
(which we could see as a new clarity of vision…at
the risk of maybe overanalyzing),

00:08:39.399 --> 00:08:45.540
Marco’s phoenix form burned again, clashing
with some of the great powers of the world

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:50.990
- the commanders of two Yonkou crews and briefly
with Big Mom herself.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:56.030
His healing powers came in clutch during the
battle and he even helped Zoro make it on

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.779
time to participate in Roof Piece.

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:03.889
Many fans also see Marco as the pheasant parallel
within the Momotaro myth, in which Momonosuke

00:09:03.889 --> 00:09:11.670
restored his kingdom with the help of a Monkey
(Luffy), Dog (Yamato), and Pheasant (Marco).

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:16.470
The phoenix played an invaluable role in the
Ninja-Pirate-Mink-Samurai alliance and likely

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.930
helped turn the tide of the battle for Wano
country.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:25.930
It’s still unknown what will become of Marco
in the final saga, but surely there’s more

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:26.930
to his story.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:31.560
As far as we know, Whitebeard’s supposed
son, Weevil, is still hunting the remnants

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.879
of the Whitebeard pirates.

00:09:32.879 --> 00:09:38.259
Will he eventually restore this crew to their
former glory, finally marking a true rebirth?

00:09:38.259 --> 00:09:42.870
Will the rest of the division commanders that
we haven’t seen post timeskip make an appearance?

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:47.079
There’s still hope, too, that the figurative
death and rebirth that Marco has followed

00:09:47.079 --> 00:09:52.649
in the story so far will be followed by a
literal death and rebirth, enabled by his

00:09:52.649 --> 00:09:55.360
mythical zoan fruit.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:03.089
In a recent video on this channel, the Phoenix
fruit was actually named the most powerful

00:10:03.089 --> 00:10:04.759
of all the zoan fruits!

00:10:04.759 --> 00:10:10.019
If you want to know the secret to why it is
the best of the best and see which fruits

00:10:10.019 --> 00:10:14.399
it narrowly beat, you really shouldn’t miss
out on that video right here.

